From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Yevhen Salitrynskyi <ysalitrynskyi@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 31 Aug 2026 23:19:14 -0400
Subject: open a command bar on Cmd+T

The reference opens a centred overlay on Cmd+T, not a blank tab: a search field
over a list of places to go, mixing tabs in the current Space with tabs in other
Spaces, each labelled with the Space it is in.

That labelling is the payoff of ADR 0015. Because every Space's tabs stay in one
TabStripModel, finding a tab in another Space is a loop over the strip rather
than a search through parked trees. Switching to one makes its Space active
first, so the tab is never activated while still hidden.

Enter takes the first result, or opens what was typed -- a URL if it fixes up to
one, and a search with the profile's own engine otherwise. Escape closes.

Two Views constraints shaped this. BubbleDialogDelegateView and
WidgetDelegateView both have private constructors and a friend list, so neither
can be subclassed from here; the bar is a plain View set as a popup widget's
contents view instead. That suits it anyway, since the overlay is centred over
the window rather than anchored to any control.

Cmd+T still opens a blank tab in popups and app windows, and whenever the
Arc-style window feature is off.

Why: Cmd+T is the most-used key in a browser and the reference makes it the way
in to everything, including other Spaces.
Removable when: never, short of dropping the command bar.
